        "target": {
          "asset_id": "arn:aws:wafv2::123456789012:webacl/prod-api",
          "asset_type": "aws_wafv2_web_acl"
        },
        "action": "Enable full request body inspection on the Web ACL and increase the body size inspection limit beyond the default 8KB to cover modern API payloads. Enable sampled request logging for allowed requests — not only blocked requests. For AWS WAF, configure the Web ACL body inspection to inspect the full body and enable request sampling via the AWS WAF console or UpdateWebACL API. Reference: HackerOne report #2921905 documents a WAF bypass via CRLF injection that would be detectable with full body inspection and request sampling."
